From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 21:20:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 58/62] verimark: fix IT list (0x9f) + delete (0xA3) via
 async-over-sync wrapper
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the failing raw bulk_out/bulk_in/decrypt sync paths with a nested
GMainContext wrapper around verimark_session_call_opcode_async — the same
path used by the runtime-validated verify and enroll SSMs.

IT delete now sends the correct 0xA3 DeleteObject opcode with the
[class=1][pad:3][TUID:16] payload (byte-identical to DT) instead of the
0xA4 partition-GC opcode, which RE confirmed cannot target a template.

IT list now reaches the BULK transport correctly (the previous code used
verimark_transport_io_bind which is CONTROL-only and does not auto-route
by PID).

Add verimark_storage_build_delete_payload as a shared DT/IT helper that
builds the 20-byte [class:1][pad:3=00 00 00][tuid:16] request payload,
with two new TDD cases asserting its byte layout.

Runtime-validated 2026-06-07 via examples/manage-prints against a real
IT (047d:8054): 8 prints listed via 0x9f, all 8 deleted via 0xA3 with
the expected cascade pattern (3-3-3-3-3-1-1-1 sensor objects, i.e. one
class-1 tuid backed by 3 internal classes, with class-2/3 entries shared
across earlier deletes already collected).

The DT path is unchanged — the new branch is gated by VERIMARK_PID_IT.
